#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example uses generic tables, CarSim keywords, and axle and vehicle side indices to describe a non-linear relationship between suspension travel (jounce) and spring seat displacement.
#
#Previously the VS Browser only supported linear coefficients to describe the suspension compliance coefficients, spring seats, and suspension mechanical ratios.
#
#This example is overlaid with the simulation "Bounce Sine Sweep". In the overlay, an identical D-Class Sedan is used on the same road, however the dataset linked on this Run Control screen for non-linear spring seats is not used.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

